`QQmlListReference::append(QObject*)` requires the object to be of the list's element type (QQuickTransform). Translate is. Good.

Note: `transforms.clear()` deletes previously appended transforms? QQmlListReference::clear() removes and may delete? It clears the list; ownership is the item? The appended objects have parent=item, so they'd be deleted when item is deleted; clear() removes references but doesn't delete the objects (they'd leak until item deletion). Acceptable. Actually, to avoid leaks on repeated sets, we could delete them; but offsets are set rarely. Fine.

