        pathland_qt_layer_apply(top.as_ptr(), top.len() as u32);
        assert!((pathland_qt_layer_padding(1, c"topMargin".as_ptr()) - 4.0).abs() < 0.5, "per-edge padding -> topMargin");
    });
}
```
`c""` literal: Rust supports c-strings via `c"..."` in edition 2021+ (stabilized 1.77). The existing code uses `c"value".as_ptr()` (I saw `c"value"` usage). So `c"".as_ptr()` works.

