Now B: reconcileZStackSize. Add after reapplyZStackAlignment, before recomputeLayout. Then call it in recomputeLayout.

```cpp
// ZStack own size (spec/PRIMITIVES.md §ZStack): a Hug ZStack sizes to the
// largest child on each axis — the maximum, never the sum. A Fill axis (or fill
// propagation) comes from `effectiveFill`/the layout, so only non-fill children
// contribute here.
void reconcileZStackSize(uint32_t id) {
    QQuickItem *item = findWidget(id);
    if (!item) {
        return;
    }
    auto ch = g.children_of.find(id);
    if (ch == g.children_of.end()) {
        return;
    }
    bool anyW = false, anyH = false;
    double maxW = 0.0, maxH = 0.0;
    for (uint32_t childId : ch->second) {
        auto cit = g.components.find(childId);
        if (cit != g.components.end() && isNonVisual(cit->second)) {
            continue;
        }
        QQuickItem *c = findWidget(childId);
        if (!c) {
            continue;
        }
        if (!effectiveFill(childId, true, false)) {
            maxW = std::max(maxW, std::max(c->implicitWidth(), c->width()));
            anyW = true;
        }
        if (!effectiveFill(childId, false, false)) {
            maxH = std::max(maxH, std::max(c->implicitHeight(), c->height()));
            anyH = true;
        }
    }
    if (anyW) {
        item->setImplicitWidth(maxW);
    }
    if (anyH) {
        item->setImplicitHeight(maxH);
    }
}
```

And in recomputeLayout's ZStack loop, call reconcileZStackSize then reapplyZStackAlignment. Order: reconcile size first (so alignment uses the box size? but box size = implicit, not width until parent layout). Actually alignment uses parent->width() which is the actual width. For a root-ish ZStack, width may be assigned by anchors. For a hug ZStack inside a layout, the layout assigns width = implicit at layout time, then widthChanged → reapply. So order within recomputeLayout doesn't matter much. Let me call reconcileZStackSize then reapplyZStackAlignment.

