parts.text:
The implicit-size logic I wrote is convoluted and buggy (it references `item->implicitWidth()` and negations that don't make sense). Let me simplify:

The viewport implicit size should be:
- If an axis is HUG_CONTENT → implicit = content size on that axis.
- Else if the axis is the CROSS axis and the content does NOT effectively fill → the viewport hugs the content: implicit = content size.
- Else (scroll axis) → greedy, implicit irrelevant (but leave as is / 0).
- If the cross axis content fills → the viewport fills via effectiveFill (parent layout), so implicit irrelevant.

Let me rewrite that block clearly:

```cpp
const bool hugW = ...HUG;
const bool hugH = ...;
const bool contentFillW = effectiveFill(contentId, true, false);
const bool contentFillH = effectiveFill(contentId, false, false);
// Cross axis is horizontal iff !scrollH? No: cross axis is horizontal iff scrollH is false.
const bool crossH = !scrollH;
double implicitW = item->implicitWidth();
double implicitH = item->implicitHeight();
if (hugW || (crossH && !contentFillW)) implicitW = content->width();
if (hugH || (!crossH && !contentFillH)) implicitH = content->height();
item->setImplicitWidth(implicitW);
item->setImplicitHeight(implicitH);
```

Wait, `crossH` = the cross axis is horizontal when the scroll axis is vertical (scrollH false). So `crossH = !scrollH`. Yes.

But if the axis is the scroll axis, we don't hug (greedy), so implicit stays. If HUG_CONTENT on the scroll axis, hug. Good.

Let me simplify and fix.

Actually, my current block:
```cpp
item->setImplicitWidth(hugW || (!scrollH && !effectiveFill(contentId, true, false)) ? content->width() : item->implicitWidth());
item->setImplicitHeight(hugH || (scrollH && !effectiveFill(contentId, false, false)) ? content->height() : item->implicitHeight());
```
`(!scrollH && !effectiveFill(contentId,true,false))` = cross horizontal (when scroll vertical) and content doesn't fill horizontal → hug width. `(scrollH && !effectiveFill(contentId,false,false))` = cross vertical (when scroll horizontal) and content doesn't fill vertical → hug height. That's actually correct! But setting `item->implicitWidth()` as the else (reading then setting) is odd but harmless. Let me rewrite for clarity.

Let me replace the block with the clearer version.

